;; drrupp.org — redirect-to-primary records ONLY
;;
;; Import this file in the Cloudflare dashboard:
;;   drrupp.org zone -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export -> Import DNS records
;;
;; SAFETY: This file is ADDITIVE. A Cloudflare import only ADDS the records
;; listed below — it never deletes or modifies existing records. This file
;; contains NO MX, NO TXT, NO SPF/DKIM/DMARC records, so importing it cannot
;; touch your email configuration.
;;
;; HOW THIS WORKS: this domain does not point at GitHub Pages directly (a
;; Pages site can only serve one custom domain). Instead, these two records
;; make Cloudflare answer for the hostname — 192.0.2.1 is a reserved
;; documentation IP that never routes anywhere — and a Redirect Rule (created
;; by hand, step 3 below) sends visitors to the live site before the dummy
;; IP is ever contacted. The cf-proxied tags below import the records as
;; Proxied (orange cloud), which is REQUIRED for the redirect to fire.
;;
;; IMPORTANT — do these by hand (see dns/README.md):
;;   1. Export a backup of the zone first.
;;   2. Before importing, delete any EXISTING A, AAAA, or CNAME records on
;;      "drrupp.org" (the apex/@) and on "www" that point at old hosting.
;;      Touch NOTHING else — leave every MX, TXT, SRV, and
;;      mail-/dkim-/dmarc-named record alone.
;;   3. After importing, create the redirect: Rules -> Redirect Rules ->
;;      Create rule -> When: All incoming requests -> Then: Dynamic redirect,
;;      expression:
;;        concat("https://cashrealestateconsulting.com", http.request.uri.path)
;;      status 302. (Point it at https://cashconsults.com instead after the
;;      cutover — see dns/README.md.)

$ORIGIN drrupp.org.
$TTL 300

;; Proxied placeholders so Cloudflare answers and the redirect rule fires
drrupp.org.	300	IN	A	192.0.2.1 ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:true
www.drrupp.org.	300	IN	A	192.0.2.1 ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:true
